## 4. UI & Component Architecture

### 4.1 Styling (Mandatory)
- **Tailwind CSS**: The primary styling solution is **Tailwind CSS**. All new components and features **must** use Tailwind utility classes.
- **shadcn/ui**: All components **must** be built using `shadcn/ui` primitives. Avoid creating new components from scratch that duplicate existing shadcn functionalities.
- **CSS Variables**: Use CSS variables for theming system
- **Responsive Design**: Use responsive design with a mobile-first approach

### 4.2 Component Patterns
- Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Use composition over prop drilling
- Implement proper error boundaries for error handling
- **Separate Positioning from Component Styling**: Use wrapper elements to separate layout/positioning concerns from component-specific styling
  - **Component classes**: Intrinsic styling (size, colors, padding, borders, accessibility enhancements)
  - **Wrapper classes**: Extrinsic positioning (absolute, relative, flex positioning, z-index, top, left, right, bottom)

**Example**:
```tsx
// ❌ Mixing positioning with component styling
<Button className="absolute bottom-4 right-4 z-10 size-9 rounded-md p-2">
  <Icon />
</Button>

// ✅ Separated concerns - positioning in wrapper, styling on component
<div className="absolute bottom-4 right-4 z-10">
  <Button className="size-9 rounded-md p-2">
    <Icon />
  </Button>
</div>
```

